# Atizar — environment example. Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill what you use.
# Official framework vars are ATIZAR_-prefixed; vendor vars (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, DATABASE_URL,
# DEV_RECORD_REPLAY, …) are read as their owners name them. This file holds NO values.

# --- Framework ---
# AES master key for the encrypted credential store (any string; required for OAuth integrations).
ATIZAR_SECRET_KEY=
# Postgres URL override (optional). Precedence: ATIZAR_DATABASE_URL > DATABASE_URL > the
# docker-compose default below — so for the standard `docker compose up -d postgres` setup you
# need set NOTHING here.
ATIZAR_DATABASE_URL=
# The compose/default Postgres URL the server, tests, and drizzle-kit fall back to (matches
# docker-compose.yml). Override only to point at a different database.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://aiworkflow:aiworkflow@localhost:5432/aiworkflow

# --- Provider (LLM) ---
# Anthropic API key for PROVIDER=mastra (vendor convention — NOT namespaced).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Google OAuth app (for Gmail and other Google integrations) ---
# One-time app registration from Google Cloud Console (APIs & Services -> Credentials -> OAuth
# client ID, type Desktop/Web). The per-user token comes from the in-app Connect flow, NOT here.
ATIZAR_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
ATIZAR_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Dev tooling ---
# Dev record/replay for the claude-cli provider (see docs/dev-record-replay.md):
#   unset   -> pure production path
#   1       -> auto (replay if a cassette exists, else record)
#   record  -> force-refresh cassettes
# DEV_RECORD_REPLAY=1
